    "definitions": {
      "short": "pasturage ; concretely, a flock",
      "usage": "flock, pasture.",
      "full": "H4830. marith [ מַרְעִית ] noun feminine pasturing, shepherding, pasturage (always figurative); — suffix מַרְעִיתִי Jer 23:1 ; Ezek 34:31 , מַרְעִיתֶ֑ךָ Psa 74:1 ; 79:13 , etc.; &#8212; 1 pasturing, shepherding , מַרְעִיתִי צאֹן , of Israel as flock of ׳י , Jer 23:1 ; Ezek 34:31 , compare Psa 74:1 ; 79:13 ; 100:3 + 95:7 (read ׳צ ׳מ יָדוֺ וְעַם , compare Hup-Now Che). 2 pasturage , Hosea 13:6 (Now כִּרְעוֺתָם ), Isa 49:9 ; Jer 25:36 . 3 by meton. = flock Jer 10:21 .",
      "rootNote": "from 7462 in the sense of feeding ;",
